# Single ignore file for the whole monorepo.
#
# Every turborepo-based image (nest-*, next, strapi, forms-shared, openapi-clients)
# builds with the repository root as its Docker context, and Docker only ever reads
# the .dockerignore at the context root. The per-package .dockerignore files are
# therefore inert -- change rules here, not there.
#
# Two caveats when editing:
#   1. Anything excluded here is also missing from `turbo prune --docker` output,
#      so it can never be recovered in a later stage.
#   2. Never exclude a directory listed in pnpm-workspace.yaml. `turbo prune` reads
#      every workspace package.json to build the dependency graph, so a missing
#      member breaks it. Narrow inside package dirs instead.

# ---- never useful in any build ----
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.turbo
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.volta
**/.claude
.github

# ---- build outputs (always regenerated inside the image) ----
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache
# Prisma's `prisma-client` generator emits a host-platform query engine binary
# here; `db:generate` regenerates it for the image platform during the build.
**/src/generated/prisma

# ---- noise ----
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.md
tests/cypress/videos
tests/cypress/screenshots

# ---- secrets: excluded by default ----
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# ---- ...except the committed, non-secret Next.js config it needs to build ----
# next/Dockerfile promotes .env.ci-build.<BUILD_ENV> to .env.production.local
# during the build, so the sources must reach the context.
!next/.env.ci-build.*
!**/.env.spec
